LC 344 — Reverse String
Pattern:

Two Pointers

Logic:
One pointer at the start
One pointer at the end
Swap them
Move both toward the middle

Algorithm:
i = 0
j = last index

while i < j:
    swap s[i], s[j]
    i++
    j--

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    void reverseString(vector<char>& s) {
        int i = 0, j = s.size() - 1;

        while (i < j) {
            swap(s[i], s[j]);
            i++;
            j--;
        }
    }
};



EX:
s = ["h","e","l","l","o"]

